WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.800
In November of 1983, The Demogorgon was banished&nbsp;
from Hawkins, and during Christmas of that year,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:09.040
12 year old William Byers coughed up a strange&nbsp;
slug that disappeared down the drain of his sink.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:12.560
The creatures of the Upside-Down would not&nbsp;
be finished with this small town quite yet.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:16.880
A new form of the Demogorgon coined as the demodog&nbsp;
has been growing its ranks in the shadows. 
 &nbsp;

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:20.880
Because the demodogs operate using a hivemind,&nbsp;
they’re able to dig a series of tunnels underneath&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:24.880
the town. Despite their mental connection, one&nbsp;
of them manages to distance itself from the rest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:28.720
of the pack and even form a bond with one of&nbsp;
the humans. To dive into the hive and see how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:32.640
the demodogs’ pack really works, and what made&nbsp;
D’Artagnan an occasional exception&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:35.280
stick around to the end of this video.
 
 &nbsp;

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:37.023
This video is sponsored by Scentbird.

00:00:37.024 --> 00:00:39.024
(metal music)

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:46.160
It’s Halloween in 1984 and the kids of&nbsp;
Hawkins, Indiana are not missing out on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:49.280
their trick-or-treating, but 13-year&nbsp;
old Dustin Henderson finds the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:53.600
surprising treat of the night in his trash can&nbsp;
foraging for food. After bringing the small,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:57.040
slimy creature inside, he believes&nbsp;
he’s discovered a species of pollywog;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:00.000
a tadpole that he expects to&nbsp;
grow into some kind of amphibian.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.840
I’ll call this stage one of the creature’s&nbsp;
metamorphosis, and just for fun, I’ll give&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:08.480
it a nickname: the demowog. Physically, it&nbsp;
looks like a slimy frog with an extended tail.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:12.160
He tries feeding it a few pieces of his 3&nbsp;
Musketeers bar and discovers that the creature&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:15.360
doesn’t like the heat lamp in the tortoise&nbsp;
tank he’s keeping it in. It hides in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:19.120
shade until Dustin turns the heat lamp off,&nbsp;
at which point it goes to munch on the candy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:22.880
Because it takes a liking to this chocolate&nbsp;
bar, Dustin names it D’Artagnan after the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:26.320
protagonist of The Three Musketeers novel,&nbsp;
D’Artagnan, but mostly just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:29.760
refers to it as “Dart” for short. We&nbsp;
don’t know if Dart is male or female,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:33.760
or if it just doesn’t doesn’t have a gender like&nbsp;
Mewtwo, but Dustin seems to think it’s a dude.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:35.280
– I gotcha little guy.

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:38.080
– It’s not yet known if this is a&nbsp;
result of digesting the chocolate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:40.320
or part of its metamorphosis, but that evening,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:43.680
Dart has some kind of violent stomach ache&nbsp;
that includes something moving around in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:47.440
it’s abdomen if you can call it that,&nbsp;
that causes it to screech out in pain.

00:01:47.788 --> 00:01:48.788
(screech)

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:52.880
Dustin brings Dart to school the next day,&nbsp;
Thursday, November 1st, in his homemade&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:57.280
Ghostbusters trap, and convinces his friends to&nbsp;
join him in the A.V. room to see his discovery.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:00.560
During class, Dart rumbles around in&nbsp;
its case and makes noises reminiscent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:04.160
of a stomach growl. That afternoon,&nbsp;
everyone takes a turn holding Dart.

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:06.080
– Uh, he’s like a living booger!

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:10.480
– I say the same thing every time someone touches&nbsp;
me in LA. They theorize that Dart is a pollywog,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:14.800
but he only seems to resemble species from&nbsp;
India and South America. Mike notices what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:18.480
looks to be something moving inside of it&nbsp;
and moves the light to get a better look.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:22.320
Dart doesn’t appreciate the direct light and&nbsp;
freaks out. The sound of the screech he makes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:25.760
causes Will to remember the Upside-Down&nbsp;
and the moment he spit out a potentially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:29.360
smaller version of Dart a year ago.
 
Unlike the known species of pollywog,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:33.760
which are cold blooded, Dart doesn’t like light&nbsp;
or heat, so believing he discovered a new species;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:36.720
Dustin and the group decide to show&nbsp;
their science teacher Mr. Clarke.

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:40.320
However after Will reveals to Mike that&nbsp;
he believes Dart is from the Upside-Down,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:43.120
they rush to stop Dustin before&nbsp;
he gets Mr. Clarke involved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:46.320
(since they made a pact with Hawkins Lab the&nbsp;
previous year that they’d keep all the stuff&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:49.920
about the Upside-Down a secret). They quickly&nbsp;
bring the container back to the A.V. room.

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:53.440
Dart rages inside of the box, causing&nbsp;
the whole thing to shake violently.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:57.440
Mike readies a heavy microphone ready in case&nbsp;
it attacks and Dustin releases the doors.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.440 --> 00:02:59.760
Instead of attacking, it screeches while its skin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:04.280
ripples. A pair of hindlegs burst from&nbsp;
its sides with a splattering of slime.

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:05.280
[CLIP]

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:08.800
It would appear that the agonizing sounds it&nbsp;
had been making had less to do with it being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:12.640
hungry and more to do with growing pains from&nbsp;
the metamorphosis. The movement they had seen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:16.400
around it’s abdomen area was most likely the&nbsp;
creature trying to kick out it’s hind legs to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:21.280
be able to move more effectively. We’ll call this&nbsp;
stage 2: the demofrog. Dart runs out the door and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:26.160
away from the danger it sensed in the room. Then&nbsp;
Dustin tackles his friend Max for no reason. LOL.
 &nbsp;

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:29.680
Dart ends up hiding in the back corner&nbsp;
of a bathroom stall. Will finds it first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:33.680
but Dart’s screeching gives Will a little&nbsp;
bit of Upside-Down PTSD. Once the door shuts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:37.280
Dart moves behind the toilet until Dustin&nbsp;
arrives doing his best Randall Boggs.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:39.280
[CLIP]

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:43.200
It would appear that Dustin was right about&nbsp;
the trust shared between himself and Dart,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:47.120
because when he finds him, Dart is willing to&nbsp;
hop into Dustin’s hands and hide under his hat.
 &nbsp;

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:50.720
After being returned to the safety of Dustin’s&nbsp;
turtle tank, Dart goes to town on some more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:54.560
3 Musketeers before falling asleep for the&nbsp;
night. Deciding Dart would be safer at home,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:57.840
Dustin leaves him in the turtle tank while&nbsp;
he goes to school the next day. Now, either&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:02.320
Dustin didn’t see Gremlins, or forgot the rules&nbsp;
about feeding strange creatures late at night,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:05.840
because he returns home to find the tank&nbsp;
broken and with some kind of molted skin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:08.240
or membrane dripping in slime left inside.

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:12.080
It’s strange that Dustin doesn’t seem to notice&nbsp;
the immediate parallels between his own situation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:16.320
with Dart and what goes on with Gizmo, the&nbsp;
titular Gremlin of Gremlins, late at night.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:20.800
Maybe he somehow missed Gremlins being in theaters&nbsp;
back in August because he went away to camp during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:24.960
the summer. Or he let his joy over discovering&nbsp;
a slimy a new friend cloud his judgement.

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:28.480
Dart grows into stage 3: the demohog.&nbsp;
Not because it looks like a hog,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:31.440
but more because he’s hogging up&nbsp;
all the food... Like Dustin’s cat.

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:35.360
Will and Mike had previously shared their worries&nbsp;
about Dart being a creature from the Upside Down,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:39.200
and this is basically confirmed here.when&nbsp;
Dart’s face opens up just like the Demogorgon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:43.840
from a year ago, canine teeth included. This is&nbsp;
also confirmed by the VFX team for the show.
 &nbsp;

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:47.520
The maturation rate of Dart shows how quickly&nbsp;
the demodogs can increase their numbers by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:52.080
using a molting process that may or may not be&nbsp;
sped up by eating certain foods. Perhaps Dustin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:57.040
realizes that as he comes up with a plan to trap&nbsp;
Dart. Using a classic trail of bologna slice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.040 --> 00:05:01.698
he lures the creature outside and yeets him&nbsp;
into the cellar. That could have gone so badly.

00:05:01.937 --> 00:05:03.520
– What gives you the right? What is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:07.120
the difference between you and me?
– [Dart with Batman voice] I’m not wearing hockey pads.

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:09.920
What makes this interesting is that&nbsp;
it’s the first time we see a creature&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:14.000
from the Upside-Down outside during&nbsp;
daylight hours. It’s also a sunny day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:17.760
which should deter Dart from leaving the&nbsp;
safety of the indoors. Maybe it’s a plot hole,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:21.280
or maybe there’s something that makes&nbsp;
Dart special in this stage 3 form.

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:25.680
– [Dart with Frieza voice] You have the esteemed privilege of&nbsp;
being the first to see my next form!

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:30.000
Locked in the cellar, Dart molts again.&nbsp;
Stage 4, as we know, is the demodog.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:34.720
– Demodogs?
– [Dustin] Demogorgon. Dogs. Demodogs.”

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:37.040
– With a stronger set of claws&nbsp;
that come with this new form,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:41.280
Dart manages to find a weak spot to dismantle&nbsp;
a corner of the wall. Once it reaches the soil,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:45.440
it’s able to dig an escape tunnel until it reaches&nbsp;
the tunnel system all underneath Hawkins. These&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:49.920
tunnels are used by the demodogs to travel while&nbsp;
staying out of both the sun and the public eye.
 &nbsp;

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:53.280
The best example of how travel efficient these&nbsp;
tunnels can be is showcased when Dustin and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:57.760
Steve Harrington are joined by Lucas and Max at&nbsp;
the junkyard to help lure Dart out and take care&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.760 --> 00:06:02.320
of it. Dart appears after night has settled in&nbsp;
and a fog has rolled across the area. But Dart&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:06.640
will not fall for the same trick twice, it doesn’t&nbsp;
move towards the pile of meat they have set up.
 &nbsp;

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:11.520
Steve believes Dart wants a different kind of&nbsp;
entrée, one seasoned with “faberge organics”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:15.920
and steps out of the reinforced bus to try and&nbsp;
provoke Dart to go after him. Little does he know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:21.200
Dart is simply a decoy while other demodogs&nbsp;
surround Steve and the bus for an ambush.&nbsp;

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:25.983
–  [Dart with Michael Scott voice] Well, well, well. How the turntables...

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:31.042
– [Zac] Outnumbering Steve, the demodogs&nbsp;
pounce towards their next meal.
 &nbsp;

