 &nbsp;

00:07:38.214 --> 00:07:42.000
(ominous music)

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:45.920
Inches away from the razor-sharp&nbsp;
claws of a ferocious pack of dogs…

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:47.440
– [Dustin] Demodogs.
– I’m sorry, what?

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:53.600
– I said demodogs. Like demogorgon and&nbsp;
dogs. You put them together. Sound pretty badass.

00:07:53.600 --> 00:07:58.800
– Inches away from the razor-sharp claws of a&nbsp;
ferocious pack of DEMOdogs, Steve makes a run for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:02.560
it. Demodogs pounce at him from all directions,&nbsp;
and one of them ends up on the wrong end of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:07.040
Steve’s best Ryne Sandberg impersonation. We’re&nbsp;
in the 80s, had to go 80s for that reference.

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:11.680
Steve gets to safety, but one of the dogs jumps&nbsp;
onto the roof of the bus and almost gets inside,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:15.840
but gets distracted by the call of another&nbsp;
demodog, or possibly something greater.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:19.760
More on that later. It’s possible that&nbsp;
this demodog on top of the bus was Dart,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:23.040
based on the yellow spots seen on the&nbsp;
tail, but it’s hard to tell for sure.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:26.240
If that is Dart, maybe it took pity&nbsp;
after seeing Dustin in the bus.

00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:30.160
It joins the rest of the hunting party and leaves&nbsp;
to follow the call of another one of its kind.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:34.880
What we can learn about the species from this, is&nbsp;
that the demodogs hunt in packs like lions and…&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:37.760
the raptors in Jurassic Park.&nbsp;
Once they have their target,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:41.360
they lunge forward, teeth-first. Like&nbsp;
most life forms from the Upside-Down,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.360 --> 00:08:45.280
it would appear that the demodogs are almost&nbsp;
like a remix of many creatures from our world.
 &nbsp;

00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:48.640
Dart’s may have been called away because of what&nbsp;
was happening at the Hawkins Lab, where a group&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.640 --> 00:08:53.040
of scientists trying to enter the Upside Down were&nbsp;
massacred by the pack. One demodog appears from a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:57.440
hole in the floor and tries bashing the protective&nbsp;
glass, but unlike Pennywise’s face that one time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.440 --> 00:09:01.680
it fails to get through, so it lets out a&nbsp;
wolflife howl, inviting the others join it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:05.440
This signal is what lured Dart and his party&nbsp;
away from the junkyard. As a group, they’re able&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:09.600
to make some progress on the glass barrier.
 
The entire pack of demodogs invade the lab&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:13.520
sending Chief Hopper and a group of scientists&nbsp;
running for their lives. As a pack, they’re able&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:17.840
to sync up their attack patterns. For example,&nbsp;
three of them tackling at once is enough to rip&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:22.160
down a steel door, allowing them to claim their&nbsp;
prize and chow down on a group of scientists.

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:26.160
Despite the fact that most of the demodogs’&nbsp;
only exposure to the Rightside-Up is limited&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.160 --> 00:09:29.920
to the underground tunnel network, they still&nbsp;
seem to have no problem navigating the halls&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:33.680
of the Hawkins Lab. Earlier I alluded&nbsp;
to the demodogs sharing a hive mind.

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:38.080
The term hive mind comes from a hive of bumble&nbsp;
bees. The queen bee emits specific hormones to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.080 --> 00:09:42.960
help coordinate the female workers and the male&nbsp;
drones. The hive mind allows information about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:46.880
water or pollen is located to be shared to&nbsp;
the entire hive to make them more efficient.
 &nbsp;

00:09:46.880 --> 00:09:51.200
The demodogs use a combination of sounds to&nbsp;
alert each other, and their “queen” is a colossal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:55.520
creature known as the Mind Flayer. The Mind&nbsp;
Flayer also has a special connection with Will,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.520 --> 00:09:59.840
essentially making him part of the hive mind. By&nbsp;
using Will to recognize where his friends were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:04.400
located, the Mind Flyer sent a group of demodogs&nbsp;
to hunt them down, so Mike has the idea to sedate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:08.400
him to prevent him from communicating with them.&nbsp;
As a result of this, the demodogs actually have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:12.080
to search for their victims, giving them&nbsp;
all time to move to the the security room.

00:10:12.080 --> 00:10:16.320
With the entire lab taken over by demodogs,&nbsp;
the group decides they need to perform a system&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.320 --> 00:10:20.800
reboot to reactivate the door locks. They send&nbsp;
a man named Bob Newby down to the breaker room.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:24.000
He arrives there and finds that every&nbsp;
lab employee in there has already been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:27.760
ripped to shreds by the creatures. He&nbsp;
is able to successfully restart the lab,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:31.920
but his friends find he is now trapped by a&nbsp;
demodog that moved into the west stairwell.

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:35.440
This, in addition to the pack using a decoy&nbsp;
against Steve Harrington earlier speaks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:38.880
to the intelligence of these creatures.&nbsp;
They’re not just like bumblebee drones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.880 --> 00:10:42.080
essentially following orders and&nbsp;
instinctually devouring prey.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:46.080
They seem to realize that the lights going on&nbsp;
means there’s someone back in the breaker room.

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:49.840
Bob’s able to divert this dog using a noise&nbsp;
created by the sprinkler system and get away&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.840 --> 00:10:53.440
as the others quietly move to the exit.&nbsp;
At this point, the pack splits up to more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:57.280
effectively search the grounds, which leads to&nbsp;
him getting caught. He manages to outrun one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.280 --> 00:11:00.480
but it’s calls to the rest of the pack&nbsp;
allow them to quickly swarm the door,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.480 --> 00:11:03.200
break it down and take Bob&nbsp;
as their midnight snack.

00:11:03.200 --> 00:11:05.760
They probably would have been better&nbsp;
off with that 3 Musketeers Bar though.

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:08.320
– "Big on chocolate, Not on fat!"

00:11:08.320 --> 00:11:11.680
– Chief Hopper tries to shoot them down,&nbsp;
but they’re also bulletproof. Luckily,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.680 --> 00:11:15.520
they’re too engrossed in their meal to care.
 
Everyone has regroups at the Byers’ house,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:18.080
where they have their realization&nbsp;
about the hive mind and determine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:22.000
the best way to beat the army of demodogs is&nbsp;
to destroy the shadow monster, which acts as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:26.160
the brain of this superorganism. They try&nbsp;
to question Will in an ambiguous location,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:30.080
but The Mind Flayer is still able to find out&nbsp;
where they are and send the demodogs their way.

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:34.640
Just as the first one shows up, so does the&nbsp;
completely overpowered psychokinetic girl, Eleven.

00:11:34.640 --> 00:11:37.600
She snaps its neck and tosses it&nbsp;
through the Byers’ window for some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.600 --> 00:11:40.240
reason. That’s actually kind of&nbsp;
rude and I hope she pays for it.

00:11:40.240 --> 00:11:44.480
The group splits up for a plan to try to break&nbsp;
the Mind Flayer’s influence on Will by closing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.480 --> 00:11:49.120
the gate to the Upside Down, where a massive&nbsp;
horde of demodogs is now festering. Steve,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:49.120 --> 00:11:51.760
Mike, Dustin, Max and Lucas stay at the house.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.760 --> 00:11:56.160
After putting the dead demodog in the&nbsp;
Byers’s freezer for… scientific purposes…

00:11:56.160 --> 00:11:58.160
–  [Steve] You’re explaining this to Mrs. Byers, alright?

00:11:58.160 --> 00:11:59.760
– [Zac] ...they realize they can use the hive mind to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.760 --> 00:12:03.000
their advantage by creating a&nbsp;
distraction so that the dogs…

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:04.000
– [Dustin] Demodogs!

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:06.400
– [Zac] ...so that the demodogs are&nbsp;
drawn away from the lab,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.400 --> 00:12:11.840
thus creating an easier path for Eleven to get&nbsp;
to the gate to the Upside-Down and destroy it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.840 --> 00:12:14.960
They plan to do this by starting&nbsp;
a fire in the underground tunnels.

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:18.560
Using Will’s map, they locate the area that&nbsp;
they think is the main hub where all the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.560 --> 00:12:22.960
upside down tentacle things are and cover it&nbsp;
with gasoline. Steve lights the area on fire,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.960 --> 00:12:26.160
which causes a great deal of pain&nbsp;
to those tentacles, and as a result,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:28.160
every creature that is part of the hivemind.

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:32.080
The demodogs at the gate all go crazy, and&nbsp;
the Mind Flayer prioritizes putting a stop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:32.080 --> 00:12:36.240
to the fire, so they all clear out of the gate&nbsp;
area. As Steve and the kids run for the exits,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:36.240 --> 00:12:39.040
they come face to face with none other than Dart.

00:12:39.637 --> 00:12:41.447
(screech)

00:12:42.136 --> 00:12:43.631
– Dart...

00:12:43.800 --> 00:12:45.800
(impact)

00:12:48.611 --> 00:12:50.611
(synth music)

00:12:52.400 --> 00:12:56.800
With the hub now on fire, Dart’s newest&nbsp;
task was to take out any danger to the pack.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:56.800 --> 00:13:00.640
By following the sounds of Dustin’s group,&nbsp;
Dart was the first to track them down and face&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:00.640 --> 00:13:05.840
the boy who betrayed him less than 36 hours&nbsp;
ago. Let’s just play it back one more time.

00:13:06.037 --> 00:13:07.302
(screech)

00:13:07.555 --> 00:13:08.960
They slowly approach each other,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:08.960 --> 00:13:13.840
and the two share a moment where Dustin apologizes&nbsp;
for knocking Dart into the cellar and offers a 3&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:13.840 --> 00:13:18.240
Musketeers to smooth things over and distract&nbsp;
him long enough for everyone else to sneak by.

00:13:18.240 --> 00:13:21.280
There are a couple of notable things&nbsp;
about this scene. The first is that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:25.200
the Mind Flayer doesn’t seem to have as much&nbsp;
control over Dart as it has over the others,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:27.680
as Dart is still able to&nbsp;
make decisions on his own.

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:31.440
The second is that it almost seems like Dart&nbsp;
is wired differently than the others, having&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:31.440 --> 00:13:36.240
developed a greater taste for chocolate than it&nbsp;
has for human flesh. Maybe Dart associates that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:40.080
taste with its youth, the same way that we
always have a preference for Mom’s home cooking.

00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:43.772
In the end, D’artagnan chose to eat the 3&nbsp;
Musketeers rather than following the Mind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:43.772 --> 00:13:48.000
Flayer’s orders, and in that sense, he lived&nbsp;
up to his namesake from the 3 Musketeers novel.

00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:52.480
One of the central themes of the novel is&nbsp;
this idea of all-for-one vs. one-for-all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:52.480 --> 00:13:55.040
and d’Artagnan is&nbsp;
forced to decide between being a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:55.040 --> 00:13:58.560
King’s musketeer or part of his group&nbsp;
of friends known as the inseparables.
 &nbsp;

00:13:58.560 --> 00:14:02.240
In Stranger Things, loyalty to the hivemind&nbsp;
represents the idea of one-for-all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:02.240 --> 00:14:07.520
but loyalty to his friend Dustin, who took him in&nbsp;
and fed him early on is an example of all-for-one.

00:14:07.520 --> 00:14:12.160
Despite Dustin’s repeated insistence that a&nbsp;
demodog is not a dog, their final meeting is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:15.760
reminiscent of the saying goodbye to&nbsp;
a beloved pet trope. Demodog or not,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:15.760 --> 00:14:18.000
Dart was a good pet and friend to Dustin.

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:22.160
When Eleven closes the gate, the Mind Flayer is&nbsp;
cut off from its hosts and Dart falls with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:22.160 --> 00:14:26.320
rest of the demodog army. With his army dead,&nbsp;
the Mind Flayer is forced to retreat, but that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:26.320 --> 00:14:30.640
doesn’t mean he’s defeated. But that’s a&nbsp;
story for another episode of Horror History.

00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:34.720
Hopefully this analysis helps add some context&nbsp;
to the coordination of the demodogs and their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:38.800
life cycle. And by the way, let me know who else&nbsp;
you’d like to see covered here on Horror History,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:38.800 --> 00:14:43.040
or what franchise you’d like to see me cover.&nbsp;
Checkout that playlist on the left for more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:47.840
Stranger Bois and remember to subscribe&nbsp;
to CZsWorld for new horrors every week,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:47.840 --> 00:14:54.521
ring the deathbell for notifications and I’ll see&nbsp;
you in the next one. Assuming we both survive.

00:14:54.521 --> 00:14:56.521
(upbeat music)

